course: dictionary
lesson: 11099
title: Wheezy: breath and sound
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Wheezy describes breathing that makes a whistling or rattling sound. It often happens when the tubes that carry air in the chest are narrow, as with asthma, a cold or an allergy. «Asthma narrows the tubes that carry air into the lungs, so breathing is hard and wheezy; a reliever inhaler opens them again.» The word wheezy tells you the breath is noisy, not smooth.
explain: Use the context to check. The sentence says breathing is hard, so wheezy must describe a breath that is difficult and makes a sound. Swap in the meaning: «breathing is hard and whistling» still makes sense, so the meaning fits.
explain: Wheezy can also describe an old machine that makes a breathy, whistling sound, such as «a wheezy old organ». The sound idea is the same, but the thing making it is different. In stories, «a wheezy laugh» or «a wheezy old dog» can suggest age or illness.
fact: Wheezy means breathing with a whistling or rattling sound.
fact: Wheezy is an adjective: wheezy, wheezier, wheeziest.
fact: Wheezy breathing often comes from narrow airways, as in asthma, a cold or an allergy.
fact: An asthma reliever inhaler opens the airways again; in Australia and New Zealand it is called a «puffer».
fact: If someone is wheezy and struggling to breathe, get an adult straight away or call emergency services.
exercise: «Asthma narrows the tubes that carry air into the lungs, so breathing is hard and wheezy.» What does wheezy describe? | Feeling very cold | Breathing that is smooth and quiet | *Breathing with a whistling or rattling sound | Eating a big meal
exercise: «A wheezy old organ» is in a story. What does wheezy describe here? | *An old machine making a breathy, whistling sound | A new organ playing loud music | A tall tree moving in the wind | A child singing in a choir
exercise: What can a child with asthma use to open the airways again? | A plaster | A bandage | A pair of warm socks | *A reliever inhaler, or a «puffer» in Australia
test: If someone is wheezy and struggling to breathe, what should you do? | Tell them to run around | *Get an adult or call emergency services | Wait and see if it goes away by itself | Give them a fizzy drink
test: What does «a wheezy old dog» suggest most? | Being very rich | Being brand new | Being very fast | *Old age or illness
exam: Which sentence uses wheezy correctly? | The wheezy sea was calm and blue all day | He wheezy kicked the ball across the park | The wheezy cake was baked for an hour | *The old radiator gave a wheezy whistle when it was switched on
